   "id": "e1",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      55.2,
      277.44,
      63.36
     ],
     "text": "In addition to morphological data from growing trials, the"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      65.28,
      244.8,
      73.92
     ],
     "text": "applicant has submitted evidence of the variety\u2019s"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      74.88,
      276.96,
      83.52
     ],
     "text": "resistance to nine pests and diseases. \u2018Prime\u2019 was found"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      84.96,
      284.64,
      92.64
     ],
     "text": "to be more resistant to Colletotrichum trifolii (anthracnose)"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      95.04,
      259.68,
      103.2
     ],
     "text": "than \u2018WL 318\u2019 according to the method of Ostazeski,"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      104.16,
      282.72,
      112.32
     ],
     "text": "Barnes and Hanson described in Crop Science 9: 351-354"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      114.24,
      276.0,
      121.92
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Prime\u2019 is more resistant to Corynebacterium insidiosum"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.48,
      124.32,
      255.36,
      132.48
     ],
     "text": "{bacterial wilt) than \u2018WL Southern Special\u2019 and tess"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      133.92,
      279.36,
      142.08
     ],
     "text": "resistant than \u2018WL 318\u2019 according to the method of Elling"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      144.0,
      272.16,
      152.64
     ],
     "text": "and Frosheiser described in Agronomy Journal 52:241-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      153.6,
      253.92,
      162.24
     ],
     "text": "242. \u2018Prime\u2019 has approximately the same degree of"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      164.16,
      280.32,
      172.32
     ],
     "text": "resistance to Fusarium oxysporum (Fusarium wilt) as \u201cWL"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      174.24,
      260.64,
      181.92
     ],
     "text": "318\u2019 and less resistance than 'WL Southern Special\u2019"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      184.32,
      250.56,
      192.96
     ],
     "text": "according to the method of Frosheiser and Barnes"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      193.92,
      278.4,
      203.04
     ],
     "text": "described in Phytopathology 68:943-946. \u2018Prime\u2019 is more"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      204.48,
      280.8,
      212.16
     ],
     "text": "resistant to Verticillium albo-atrum (Verticillium wilt} than"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.92,
      212.16,
      282.24,
      224.64
     ],
     "text": "\"WL 318\u2019 according to the method of Peaden described on"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      224.16,
      277.92,
      232.8
     ],
     "text": "p. 26 of USDA-ARS Misc. Pub. #1434, 1984. \u2018Prime\u2019 has"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      234.24,
      239.52,
      242.4
     ],
     "text": "approximately the same degree of resistance to"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      243.84,
      286.56,
      252.48
     ],
     "text": "Phythophthora megasperma (Phytophthora root rot) as \u2018WL"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      253.44,
      260.64,
      262.08
     ],
     "text": "Southern Special\u2019 and less resistance than \u2018WL 318\u00b0"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      264.0,
      250.56,
      272.16
     ],
     "text": "according to the method of Frosheiser and Barnes"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      273.12,
      270.24,
      281.76
     ],
     "text": "described in Crop Science 13:735-738. \u2018Prime\u2019 is more"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      283.2,
      284.16,
      291.36
     ],
     "text": "resistant to Ditylenchus dipsaci (stem nematode) than \u2018WL"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      293.28,
      285.6,
      301.92
     ],
     "text": "318\u2019 and slightly less resistant than \u2018WL Southern Special\u2019"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      303.36,
      261.12,
      311.52
     ],
     "text": "according to the method of Eljin, Evans and Faulkner"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      48.96,
      313.44,
      272.64,
      321.6
     ],
     "text": "described in Crop Science 15: 275-276. \u2018Prime\u2019 is more"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      323.52,
      281.28,
      331.68
     ],
     "text": "resistant to Acyrthosiphon kondo/ (blue alfalfa aphid) than"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      333.6,
      259.2,
      341.76
     ],
     "text": "\u201cWL 318\u2019 and has approximately the same degree of"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      49.44,
      343.68,
      262.56,
      351.84
     ],
     "text": "resistance as \u2018WL Southern Special\u2019 according to the"
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "In addition to morphological data from growing trials, the\napplicant has submitted evidence of the variety\u2019s\nresistance to nine pests and diseases. \u2018Prime\u2019 was found\nto be more resistant to Colletotrichum trifolii (anthracnose)\nthan \u2018WL 318\u2019 according to the method of Ostazeski,\nBarnes and Hanson described in Crop Science 9: 351-354\n\u2018Prime\u2019 is more resistant to Corynebacterium insidiosum\n{bacterial wilt) than \u2018WL Southern Special\u2019 and tess\nresistant than \u2018WL 318\u2019 according to the method of Elling\nand Frosheiser described in Agronomy Journal 52:241-\n242. \u2018Prime\u2019 has approximately the same degree of\nresistance to Fusarium oxysporum (Fusarium wilt) as \u201cWL\n318\u2019 and less resistance than 'WL Southern Special\u2019\naccording to the method of Frosheiser and Barnes\ndescribed in Phytopathology 68:943-946. \u2018Prime\u2019 is more\nresistant to Verticillium albo-atrum (Verticillium wilt} than\n\"WL 318\u2019 according to the method of Peaden described on\np. 26 of USDA-ARS Misc. Pub. #1434, 1984. \u2018Prime\u2019 has\napproximately the same degree of resistance to\nPhythophthora megasperma (Phytophthora root rot) as \u2018WL\nSouthern Special\u2019 and less resistance than \u2018WL 318\u00b0\naccording to the method of Frosheiser and Barnes\ndescribed in Crop Science 13:735-738. \u2018Prime\u2019 is more\nresistant to Ditylenchus dipsaci (stem nematode) than \u2018WL\n318\u2019 and slightly less resistant than \u2018WL Southern Special\u2019\naccording to the method of Eljin, Evans and Faulkner\ndescribed in Crop Science 15: 275-276. \u2018Prime\u2019 is more\nresistant to Acyrthosiphon kondo/ (blue alfalfa aphid) than\n\u201cWL 318\u2019 and has approximately the same degree of\nresistance as \u2018WL Southern Special\u2019 according to the",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
